CorrectiveAction_Q2:
The Boards/ Council for the following four Entities will be constituted on or before 31 December 2024:
Boxing SA;
National Film and  Video Foundation ( NFVF);
National Museum;
KwaZulu-Natal Museum

PanSALB: The appointment of the Board is not yet finalised and is contingent to Parliamentary processes which the Department has already initiated. To close the governance vacuum, departmental officials were seconded to be acting CEOs in Boxing SA and  NFVF. 
In PANSLAB and the National Museum, the CEOs were appointed as the acting  Accounting Authorities. 
Furthermore, the Director of the KwaZulu-Natal Museum was appointed as the Accounting Authority.

ReasonforDeviation_Q1:
The SAPS 
has established 20 EITTs in priority areas of the provinces, with eighteen at the district level and two at the provincial level.
The following areas are the primary focus of the EITTs: 
• Essential infrastructure crimes, such as the tampering, damaging, or destruction of infrastructure related to energy, transport, water, sanitation and communication services;
• Critical infrastructure crimes, such as pipeline fuel theft, extortion and robbery at construction and economic sites;
• Combating illegal mining and illicit trafficking of controlled metals, such as precious metals, copper, aluminium and chrome.
